<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/blockade> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The strategy of stopping an enemy pawn, above all a passed or isolated pawn, by planting a piece on the square directly in front of it; systematised by Aron Nimzowitsch, who held that a pawn should be physically blocked rather than merely watched." .
