<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/chess960> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chess variant devised by Bobby Fischer in which the pieces on the back rank are shuffled before each game, under constraints that keep castling possible and the bishops on opposite colours, giving 960 possible starting positions; all other rules are those of standard chess." .
