<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/emanuel-lasker> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "German master (1868–1941) and the second official world chess champion, who took the title from Wilhelm Steinitz in 1894 and held it for 27 years until losing to José Raúl Capablanca in 1921, the longest reign in the championship's history; also a mathematician known for his work on ideals." .
