<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/ruy-lopez> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An open game arising after 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5, in which White develops the king's bishop to attack the knight that defends e5, preparing quick castling and a later central advance; it is the most frequently played continuation after 1.e4 e5." .
